Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.24,0:00:05.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}\N{\c&Hff8352&}Dive deep into serious learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.16,0:00:06.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}and get excited!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Witness a miracle born from fossils.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.10,0:00:14.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Once upon a time, in a certain place...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.86,0:00:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Prehistoric creatures full of personality!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.58,0:00:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Tirano, Stego, Ammonite,Trilobite.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.08,0:00:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}They've been saying "hi" for 500 million years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.00,0:00:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Prehistory! Everybody Say (Roar!)
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.20,0:00:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Ancient, Alright! Future, FLY High!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.68,0:00:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}A herd of mammoths! Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.50,0:00:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Thud thud thud thud! On your marks, get set, go!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.16,0:00:44.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Dive deep into serious learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.10,0:00:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}and get excited!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.08,0:00:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Witness a miracle born from fossils.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.80,0:00:51.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Dive deep into serious learning,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.75,0:00:53.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Playing for real.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.70,0:00:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}The universe begins with passion.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.30,0:01:00.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS\c&Hff8352&}Super happy!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.05,0:01:03.92,titulo do ep,,0,0,0,,{\b1}{\an3}Serious Dunkleosteus Comedy Contest
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.95,0:01:01.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Kanna-san,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.30,0:01:04.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}let me walk you to the clubroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.59,0:01:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I told you I'm not going!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.43,0:01:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Zebras and lions live in herds, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.43,0:01:13.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I am neither a zebra nor a lion!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.05,0:01:18.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}BEHOLD!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.13,0:01:20.78,Default,,0,0,0,,The excavated skull of Dunkleosteus!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.10,0:01:24.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}W-What's up with you all of a sudden?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.94,0:01:26.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}It's just the head, but its body must have been huge too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.32,0:01:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}but its body must have been huge too.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.58,0:01:28.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.45,0:01:33.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Dunkleosteus was the top marine predator of the Late Devonian period,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.01,0:01:36.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}but only head bones have been found,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.05,0:01:39.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}so its exact body shape and size remain unknown!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.28,0:01:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}And so, today's topic is...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.05,0:01:45.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}THE WORLD OF SERIOUS PALEONTOLOGY!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.40,0:01:50.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Again?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.10,0:01:53.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Whoa!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.60,0:01:55.91,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS} The ocean?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.73,0:01:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.42,0:01:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}We're drowning!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.40,0:02:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}This is the sea of the Devonian period!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.45,0:02:04.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Wow, amazing!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.43,0:02:05.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}How are you two talking normally under water?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.21,0:02:07.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Now then,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.84,0:02:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}draw what you think Dunkleosteus's body looked like on this skull
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.58,0:02:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Why did this turn into a comedy drawing segment?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.65,0:02:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Done!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.05,0:02:14.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}That was fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.56,0:02:15.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Let's see, Dino-kun...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.17,0:02:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}It looks like a Great White Shark!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.77,0:02:19.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Splendid!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.28,0:02:21.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Around 2017,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.43,0:02:24.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Dunkleosteus was hypothesized to resemble sharks!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.97,0:02:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Its bite force was twice that of a Great White!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.99,0:02:31.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}The part that looks like teeth is actually modified bone used to slice meat!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.31,0:02:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Hey, that's way too much info!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.29,0:02:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}How did you cram all that in your drawing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.35,0:02:36.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Since that was a great answer,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.95,0:02:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}here's a trilobite fossil for you, Dino-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.32,0:02:40.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Thank you very much!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.78,0:02:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Alright,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.18,0:02:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}next is Kanna-kun,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.50,0:02:43.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}go ahead!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.15,0:02:44.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}EH? Me?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.55,0:02:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Go on,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.92,0:02:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Kanna-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.25,0:02:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Don't look at me like that...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.11,0:02:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I'll just draw something random.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.72,0:02:52.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Here,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.29,0:02:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}take this!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.29,0:02:57.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Kanna-kun, that is...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.30,0:03:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I kind of made a joke out of it...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.83,0:03:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}MARVELOUS!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.34,0:03:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Did you already know that Dunkleosteus had a head
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.50,0:03:07.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}and shoulder area heavily covered in dense armor plate?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.72,0:03:08.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}So,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.28,0:03:12.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Kanna-san drew the skull shaped like suit of armor based on that fact?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.54,0:03:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Indeed!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.31,0:03:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}as expected of Kanna-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.72,0:03:16.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}No, no, no! There's no deep meaning behind it at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.25,0:03:19.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Sensational answers from both of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.83,0:03:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I'm telling you, it was a total coincidence!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.64,0:03:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}President Tetori, please tell us the actual answer!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.26,0:03:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Very well!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.22,0:03:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Here is the actual answer!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.35,0:03:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}In the past, based on head size, it was estimated to be 10 meters long.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.01,0:03:37.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Recent studies suggest an average length of around 3.5 meters!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.37,0:03:40.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Its jaw force was extraordinarily powerful,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.27,0:03:43.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}crushing prey like Coelacanths.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.82,0:03:49.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Furthermore, it could open its mouth
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.57,0:03:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}in 0.02 seconds and close it in 0.06 seconds!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.95,0:03:59.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}With such bite force and high-speed jaw opening,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.49,0:04:05.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Dunkleosteus reigned supreme as the apex predator of ancient oceans!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.68,0:04:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Well, pretty amazing, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.83,0:04:14.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}If there's a current consensus theory,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.16,0:04:16.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}why didn't you just tell us that from the beginning?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.55,0:04:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}It's the mainstream theory,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.60,0:04:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}but nothing is set in stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.44,0:04:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}If new fossils are discovered,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.80,0:04:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}its shape could change again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.06,0:04:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}That's the beauty and romance of paleontology!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.69,0:04:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I see!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.48,0:04:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}So President wanted to teach us that...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.16,0:04:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}How ridiculous.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.40,0:04:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I'm going home!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.23,0:04:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Wait a moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.69,0:04:36.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.91,0:04:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}WHAT IS IT?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.79,0:04:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}Since Kanna-kun's answer was so marvelous,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.07,0:04:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}here is the trilobite fossil I forgot to hand over!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.55,0:04:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS} Please accept it!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.30,0:04:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}That's amazing, Kanna-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.26,0:04:57.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnTrebuchet MS}I don't want it.
